A(('table', dict(key='kinds', caption='Single-agent and audited repair by disruption type (ε = 0.02, test split)', header=['Disruption', 'Episodes', 'Load', 'Region size', 'Feasible, single', 'Feasible, team', 'Tokens, single', 'Tokens, team'], rows=rows, widths=[1500, 1000, 800, 1000, 1100, 1100, 1100, 1100], font_half_points=16, note='Load is the mean number of constraints to re-check in the affected region. Feasible = share of repairs satisfying all constraints.')))
A(('p', f"""At ε = 0.02, the single agent repaired {E.capture(pct(feasA), 'build_manuscript.py:117: pct(feasA)', '', -1)} of the {E.capture(N_TEST_PER_SETTING, 'build_manuscript.py:117: N_TEST_PER_SETTING', f',', -1)} test repair episodes feasibly, and the audited pair {E.capture(pct(feasT), 'build_manuscript.py:117: pct(feasT)', '', -1)} ({{T:kinds}}). The audit raised tokens from {E.capture(tokA, 'build_manuscript.py:117: tokA', f'.0f', -1)} to {E.capture(tokT, 'build_manuscript.py:117: tokT', f'.0f', -1)} per disruption. Among feasible repairs, mean makespan was {E.capture(100 * gapA, 'build_manuscript.py:117: 100 * gapA', f'.1f', -1)}% above the CP-SAT incumbent for the single agent and {E.capture(100 * gapT, 'build_manuscript.py:117: 100 * gapT', f'.1f', -1)}% for the team, so the evidence supports feasibility improvement without a demonstrated makespan advantage. Feasibility fell with the size of the disruption: {E.capture(pct(bk.loc['local'].feasA), "build_manuscript.py:117: pct(bk.loc['local'].feasA)", '', -1)} (local), {E.capture(pct(bk.loc['dependency'].feasA), "build_manuscript.py:117: pct(bk.loc['dependency'].feasA)", '', -1)} (dependency) and {E.capture(pct(bk.loc['cascade'].feasA), "build_manuscript.py:117: pct(bk.loc['cascade'].feasA)", '', -1)} (cascade) for the single agent."""))
A(('h2', '4.2. Can the constraint difference predict failure?'))
